  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing sector obligated $5.3B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The sector recorded 9,140 awards with an average award size of $579K. Obligations fell 55.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $5.2B of the FY2026 to date total. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $79.8M, and the Department of Commerce follows with $7.1M. RTX CORPORATION is the largest vendor with $1.6B in obligations, followed by GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY with $1.2B and ROLLS-ROYCE CORPORATION with $803M. Historical year-by-year totals show peaks and troughs: FY21 was $7.3B, FY22 was $11.1B, FY23 was $13.7B, FY24 was $8.4B, FY25 was $12B, and FY26 is $5.3B to date. The data are current through the fiscal year to date and reflect contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing sector obligated $5.3B in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 55.9% year over year. Fiscal history shows FY25 obligations were $12B, and FY24 obligations were $8.4B. FY23 obligations were $13.7B, FY22 obligations were $11.1B, and FY21 obligations were $7.3B."
